{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017MWH3caMsQqoKZ5tvrPEmH","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have the exact format from both recent reports. Here's my findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nI found **two complete imagined_experiments.yaml files** under the \"best\" tier in recent dream reports:\n\n1. **Most recent complete report**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T011810/best/imagined_experiments.yaml`\n2. **Previous report**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T222933/best/imagined_experiments.yaml`\n\n## Exact Format Used\n\nThe **imagined_experiments.yaml** files follow this YAML structure:\n\n**Root level fields:**\n- `tier` (string): Always \"best\" in these files\n- `narrative_guidance` (string): Extended prose explaining the framing, how claims generalize, and key insights (typically 200-500 words in Chinese with domain-specific technical terminology)\n- `imagined_experiments` (array): List of experiment specifications\n\n**Per-experiment structure** (array items):\n- `name` (string): Human-readable experiment title\n- `plan_id` (string): Identifier like \"plan_012\", \"plan_010\"\n- `description` (string): Prose description of what the experiment does\n- `expected_results` (dict): Extensive key-value pairs with numeric metrics\n  - Includes: RSA scores, bootstrap CIs, p-values, effect sizes, layer-wise metrics, orderings, deltas\n  - Values can be: floats, integers, lists (for confidence intervals), strings (for orderings/rationales)\n- `result_rationale` (string): Detailed explanation of why results take this form, mechanistic insights (300-800 words typically)\n- `tables` (array): List of table specifications\n  - Each has: `title`, `columns` (array of strings), `rows` or `rows_description`\n- `figures_description` (array): Prose description of expected figure outputs (bar charts, scatter plots, curves)\n- `analysis` (string): Synthesis connecting results to the paper's claims and broader impact\n\n**Data types observed:**\n- Numeric confidence intervals as lists: `[0.47, 0.63]` (floats)\n- Boolean/ternary outcomes as strings: `\"Yes\"`, `\"No\"`, `true`, `false`\n- Ordering strings with annotations: `\"SigLIP (0.615) > CLIP (0.553) > DINO (0.388)\"`\n- ISO timestamps in filename only (not in file content)\n\nThe format emphasizes **narrativity and mechanistic explanation** at every level—from guidance through result rationale to analysis—rather than pure data serialization."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d06c3c7-e82a-4ef9-aa2a-8fa977f688e7","uuid":"eaf3894d-9a4c-485b-9207-3aae13ecc2e6","timestamp":"2026-05-22T02:22:47.330Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/, find the most recent dream report's imagined_experiments.yaml files. I need to see the exact format used. Read the content of any imagined_experiments.yaml under the \"best\" tier. Search breadth: medium.","agentId":"aec7168457631817d","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have the exact format from both recent reports. Here's my findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nI found **two complete imagined_experiments.yaml files** under the \"best\" tier in recent dream reports:\n\n1. **Most recent complete report**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T011810/best/imagined_experiments.yaml`\n2. **Previous report**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T222933/best/imagined_experiments.yaml`\n\n## Exact Format Used\n\nThe **imagined_experiments.yaml** files follow this YAML structure:\n\n**Root level fields:**\n- `tier` (string): Always \"best\" in these files\n- `narrative_guidance` (string): 